repo/docs/specs/spawn-board/design.md:402:**Auth model:** `requiresAuth: 'admin'` checks for ANY admin role (owner / global_admin / any agent_group_id admin) — not scoped per-group, because the intercept runs before we know which agent group the user is even targeting. `/dashboard-token` is admin-only because dashboard auth carries write access (steer); allowing non-admins to issue tokens would let them sign in and then 403 on every write. Better to deny issuance.
repo/docs/specs/spawn-board/design.md:404:**Reply path:** the handler writes its DM reply to the user's resolved messaging_group via the standard outbound delivery system (`writeOutboundForMessagingGroup` or equivalent — same path Slack/Discord adapters use to reply). For the host-side `/dashboard-token` flow, this means the message comes from "the host" rather than a specific agent — operator sees it as a system DM, which matches the chat-side bot conventions.
repo/docs/specs/spawn-board/design.md:408:**ASSERT (cycle-2 fix M2):** for any inbound message resolving to multiple wired agents, the intercept gate fires AT MOST ONCE per inbound message. Reviewers verify by triggering `/dashboard-token` in a DM wired to ≥2 agent groups and confirming exactly 1 row in `dashboard_tokens` results.
